[Music]  this is your tech news briefing for  thursday july 14th i'm zoe thomas for  the wall street journal  as crypto prices have plunged and  questions have been raised about the  viability of some crypto lenders and  brokers  another kind of company connected to the  crypto space has been hurt  web 3 businesses that offer their own  digital tokens  investors poured four and a half billion  dollars into blockchain-based companies  last year according to crunchbase  but games like axi infinity where  players earn assets like virtual pets  they can sell or blockchain based  fitness apps like step in where users  earn tokens based on how much they jog  have seen the value of their digital  assets crash  it raises the question if investors see  less value in bitcoin and other digital  currencies how much is a token one in a  video game worth  joining us to discuss how these startups  are coping and what it means for the  development of web 3 is our startups and  venture capital reporter berber gin  hi berber thanks for coming on the show  hi zoe very excited to be here  so let's start with the investors who  poured so much money into this over the  last year or so  how are they reacting to these companies  now that we're seeing declines in crypto  values yeah that's a great question i  think  last year  because there was so much enthusiasm  amongst just normal people  for these games what happened was that a  lot of the prices of crypto tokens went  up and so users piled into the games  they wanted to play  but they didn't necessarily use these  web three  services because they really liked in  actually infinity's case the game itself  it's because they wanted to make money  so what's happening now is as the crypto  market crashes people are sort of  fleeing from a lot of these  projects that were built on the  blockchain  and as a result investors are in a  really tricky situation last year they  sort of bought into a lot of the hype  around these startups and failed to  distinguish between companies that  actually had products that people wanted  to use  and companies that offered services that  people used because they could speculate  on assets and make a lot of money so a  lot of investors now i think are  rethinking their strategy for investing  in the space  and what they're having trouble  discerning is how much of the crypto  market actually  can offer users a better alternative to  existing social media networks games  that are already on the internet and  which types of companies are fueled  mostly by speculation of these digital  tokens which drove up the valuations and  the prices venture capitalists are  willing to pay for companies last year  right so what's the hype and and what's  i guess you know the real secret sauce  seems to be what they're figuring out so  how are the companies then addressing  that how are they trying to say we're  the real deal  yeah so that's an interesting question i  mean with axiomfinity  the company realized that  they were having trouble striking a  balance between users who wanted to play  the game and  a larger cohort of users who were  playing the game to make money  and so what they've done is actually  they're going to roll out a new version  of the game that doesn't require users  to actually own cryptocurrency assets  i think that is a really clear  indication that a lot of these so-called  web3 startups are still figuring out  whether they can  you know attract users and offer a  product that they want beyond the sort  of incentives that come with being able  to make a quick buck off some of these  tokens that  the startups issue so i think a lot of  these sort of web 3 startups that  issue digital tokens on the blockchain  to try and acquire users are in this  tougher spot now of  you know having to develop products that  people will feel attached to beyond the  money that they can make from playing  those games  how are crypto skeptics reacting to this  are they just jumping for joy and saying  i told you so  i think so i think last year because  there was so much money and hype pouring  into the space you know vcs were like  changing their twitter handles to like  nfts and adding ethereum addresses to  their usernames  last year that sort of environment made  vcs who were skeptical of crypto sort of  more hesitant to speak out  now given the crypto crash and the  general slowdown in vc investing  a lot more  vcs traditional vcs that aren't sort of  all in on crypto have been  more open about their reservations about  the space and it's definitely created  uh bifurcation within silicon valley  there are a set of vcs that are  extremely  bullish on crypto there are a set of vcs  that  you know don't want to touch it at all a  lot of them are also just investing in  sort of  safer crypto companies like  infrastructure type startups that  help other services build on the  blockchain or crypto exchanges that  facilitate trading but actually very few  vcs i think are pouring money into like  the actual projects  that are trying to supplant some of the  traditional consumer internet services  that's the sort of founding block or the  reason why crypto's supposedly so  useful in the first place but actually  not a lot of vcs have put money into  those companies  so does the the crypto rut that and some  of these vcs pulling their money away  from digital tokens spell the end of web  3.  so one way to look at this is just  from the amount of capital that's been  raised dedicated to crypto investing  i'm thinking of you know three of the  largest crypto specific funds andreessen  horowitz paradigm and han ventures  they have over eight billion dollars  dedicated to crypto investing  so from that perspective funding for  crypto startups and web 3 startups will  continue it'll probably be  a lot slower than it was last year  and there is an open question of whether  there is actually a big enough market  to  invest all that capital so if you're a  crypto skeptic who thinks that  much of the industry is fueled by you  know retail traders who  like speculating on risky assets you  might believe that this sort of spells  the beginning of the end for crypto  projects but  just by the virtue of the amount of  capital that's been reserved to help  fund and get these projects off the  ground  we're going to see more crypto and web 3  companies getting funded in the coming  years  all right that's our reporter berber gin  thanks so much for joining us berber  thank you very much  and that's it for today's tech news  briefing if you want more tech stories  check out our website wsj.com  and if you like our show please rate and  review it you can do that wherever you  get your podcasts  i'm zoe thomas for the wall street  journal  thanks for listening  [Music]  you

